\par
{\f1\fs22\b\cf1 4.  Privacy Policy}\par
{\f1\fs18\cf1 VaultMate is designed with privacy as a core principle.}\par
\par
{\f1\fs20\b\cf1 4.1  What We Collect}\par
{\f1\fs18\cf1 VaultMate collects {\b no personal data}. The application operates entirely offline. No telemetry, analytics, crash reports, or usage data are collected or transmitted. The software does not require an account, email address, or internet connection to function.}\par
\par
{\f1\fs20\b\cf1 4.2  Local Database}\par
{\f1\fs18\cf1 All data stored by VaultMate is written to a local SQLite database on your device at:\par
{\f2\fs16  %APPDATA%\\vaultmate\\vaultmate.db}\par
This file is owned entirely by you. VaultMate has no access to this file outside of your device.}\par
\par
{\f1\fs20\b\cf1 4.3  MCP Server Integration}\par
{\f1\fs18\cf1 When the built-in MCP (Model Context Protocol) server is enabled, VaultMate exposes a local network interface that AI tools on the same device can query. This interface is bound to localhost only. No data leaves your machine through this interface.}\par
\par
{\f1\fs20\b\cf1 4.4  Third-Party Services}\par
{\f1\fs18\cf1 VaultMate does not integrate with or transmit data to any third-party analytics, advertising, or tracking services.}\par
